WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.130
Every autumn, some Jewish
families build a hut outdoors,

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.700
and for a week they eat their meals in it.

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.440
It is not meant to last.

4
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.610
It is built to be temporary.

5
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.190
In winter, other families place
lights in a window for eight nights.

6
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.620
Both festivals remember very old stories.

7
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.700
How can a festival keep a story alive?

8
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.690
In this mission, you'll look closely at
how at least one of these festivals is

9
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.820
kept, and what each part of it remembers.

10
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.840
Then you'll see how
different Jews keep it today,

11
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.790
and how it has changed in modern times.

12
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.700
Your mission: find out how a festival
can keep an ancient story alive by having

13
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.090
people act it out.
